.TH RANMA-KEYS 7 "" "ranma 0.1.0" "ranma manual"
.SH NAME
ranma\-keys \- the default keys
.SH DESCRIPTION
These are the keys ranma binds before your \fIinit.lua\fR runs, as its which\-key hint
shows them; \fBranma \-\-dump\-config\fR prints the binds themselves. Rebind a key to
override it, \fBranma.unbind\fR it to drop it (a folder's key takes its keys with it).
.PP
Press the leader, \fBctrl+b\fR, to enter WM mode; the keys below are pressed in it.
WM mode stays until \fBesc\fR unless \fIwm_mode.sticky\fR is off. The leader again sends
it to the program. In WM mode, \fB?\fR lists every bind, filterable, and \fB:\fR every action.
.SH NOTATION
A capital letter is that letter with Shift (\fBM\fR is shift+m). \fB\(<-\(da\(ua\(->\fR
are the arrows, one action in four directions; \fB1\-0\fR the number row, workspaces 1 to 10;
\fB⏎\fR is Return, \fBbksp\fR Backspace, \fBDel\fR Delete, \fBspc\fR Space. Two keys
with a slash or a space between them (\fBctrl+h/l\fR, \fB( )\fR) are previous and next.
A name starting with \fB+\fR is a folder: its key opens more keys, listed under FOLDERS.
